  "observations": {
    "whatHappened": "The magnesium fizzed and shrank as bubbles streamed off it, and the tube felt warm. The collected gas burned with a squeaky pop.",
    "why": "Magnesium is more reactive than hydrogen, so it pushes hydrogen out of the acid. The metal becomes Mg²⁺ ions in solution and hydrogen gas bubbles off. The reaction gives out heat. Hydrogen mixed with air burns very fast, which makes the pop.",
